<title>AUSTRALIA: GOLF-HEINEKEN CLASSIC FINAL ROUND SCORES.</title>
<headline>GOLF-HEINEKEN CLASSIC FINAL ROUND SCORES.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH, Australia 1997-02-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading final round</p>
<p>scores and totals from the A$1.2 million ($924,000) Heineken</p>
<p>Classic golf tournament at the par-72 Vines Resort course on</p>
<p>Sunday (Australian unless stated):</p>
<p>273 Miguel Angel Martin (Spain) 70 67 65 71</p>
<p>274 Fred Couples (U.S.) 68 70 69 67</p>
<p>275 Frank Nobilo (New Zealand) 66 69 70 70, Marc Farry</p>
<p>(France) 72 66 69 68, Jean van de Velde (France)</p>
<p>69 69 69 68</p>
<p>276 Wayne Riley 71 66 69 70, Ian Woosnam (Britain)</p>
<p>72 69 69 66</p>
<p>277 Katsuyoshi Tomori (Japan) 69 68 69 71, Robert Allenby</p>
<p>70 68 71 68, Ernie Els (South Africa) 73 71 68 65</p>
<p>278 Paul Eales (Britain) 70 69 67 72, Padraig Harrington</p>
<p>(Ireland) 70 63 73 72, Rodney Pampling 68 73 66 71,</p>
<p>Greg Turner (New Zealand) 65 71 72 70, Greg Chalmers</p>
<p>70 72 71 65</p>
<p>279 Peter O'Malley 68 69 71 71, Rodger Davis 71 72 68 68</p>
<p>280 Peter Senior 69 71 70 70, David Carter (Britain)</p>
<p>71 69 70 70, Kenny Druce 71 69 72 68, Roger Chapman</p>
<p>(Britain) 70 69 73 68</p>
<p>Other scores:</p>
<p>281 Colin Montgomerie (Britain) 70 72 72 67, Andrew Coltart</p>
<p>(Britain) 71 72 69 69</p>
<p>282 Thomas Bjorn (Denmark) 69 70 74 69, Paul Broadhurst</p>
<p>(Britain) 70 69 70 73</p>
<p>302 John Daly (U.S.) 70 73 83 76.</p>
</text>
